course: dictionary
lesson: 7162
title: Periodic: happening again and again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Periodic means happening again and again, at regular times or now and then. Look at the words around it for clues. «Nurse Amira makes periodic visits to the school.» Visits that come back again and again, at set times, must be what periodic means.
explain: Periodic also has a special science meaning. «Elements in the periodic table are in order of the number of protons in their atoms.» Here periodic is part of a name, periodic table. It is a fixed name for one special chart, so learn the phrase as one thing.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The big chart of coloured squares on the science-classroom wall is the periodic table, and every square is one element.» If you swap in «the chart of all the elements», the sentence still makes sense, so you know the periodic table is a chart.
fact: Periodic means happening again and again, at regular times or now and then.
fact: «Periodic checks» are checks that happen at regular times.
fact: The «periodic table» is a chart that lists all the chemical elements in order.
fact: «Periodically» is the adverb form: it means at regular times, or now and then.
fact: Dmitri Mendeleev arranged the elements into the periodic table, left gaps for elements not yet found, and predicted them; they were found later.
exercise: «The nurse makes periodic visits to the school.» What does periodic mean here? | Very loud and sudden | Happening only once, on one special day | Made of metal | *Happening again and again, at regular times
exercise: «Hydrogen and oxygen are on the periodic table.» What is the periodic table? | A long list of school timetables | *A chart listing all the chemical elements in order | A type of pet that lives in water | A map of the playground
exercise: «Every square on the chart is one element.» Find and copy one word that names a basic substance like gold or oxygen. | square | chart | every | *element
test: «The science lesson showed the periodic table on the wall.» What is the periodic table? | *A chart of all the elements in order | A kind of weather that comes every year | A game played in the gym | The sound the school bell makes
test: «The days of the week come round in a periodic pattern.» What does periodic suggest? | Random and one-off | *Repeating again and again | Very, very fast | Sleeping through the night
exam: «Mr Patel carries out periodic checks on the lab equipment.» Which word tells you the checks happen at regular times? | *Periodic | Equipment | Checks | Lab
